@title OlliOlli tutorial - Pushing lesson
@game  PCSE00341
@shot-every 40   # in-game shots through the run so a human can assess render quality

# ============================================================================
# WHAT THIS RECIPE DOES
# Navigates the forced first-launch tutorial to the "Pushing" lesson and clears
# it. A save-less first launch routes straight into the tutorial, so this is the
# entry point every deeper OlliOlli recipe builds on.
#
# HOW IT WAS AUTHORED (lessons for the next agent)
# - The front-end is TOUCH, not buttons: menu items are hit-tested on the front
#   touch panel. Panel coords are screen*2 (front panel 1920x1088, screen
#   960x544). A tap is a sticky touch=X,Y on one line then a later line drops it.
# - Gameplay is BUTTONS: X (cross) both PUSHES on the ground and LANDS in the
#   air. "Two pushes reach full speed", so a steady X-tap cadence carries the
#   skater to the goal. No trick/land timing is needed in THIS lesson (that is
#   The Basics), which is why Pushing is the reliable warm-up.
# - The nav tap frames below were tuned on the native `play` binary (which
#   renders PNGs you can eyeball via --shots) and then hold verbatim on desktop
#   and in the browser, because a recipe is keyed on display flips, not wall
#   time. If a tap misses after an engine change, re-eyeball with --shots.
# ============================================================================

@watch vpos i32 0x81502058   # skater vertical: 60 on the ground, negative airborne,
                             # returns through 60 at touchdown. The landing-timing
                             # signal for the trick lessons; here it just confirms the
                             # skater is grounded and rolling.

# --- navigate the touch front-end to the Pushing lesson ---
0: @section navigate
12: touch=450,674     # "Offline Mode" -> dismiss the "Get yourself connected" dialog
19:
30: touch=230,230     # into the tutorial (a save-less first launch is forced here)
37:
80: touch=930,674     # OK on the "Let's learn to Skate" intro dialog
87:
112: touch=1620,376   # tutorial list
121:
128: touch=630,870    # "Pushing" -> load the lesson
137:

# --- clear the lesson: rhythmic X pushes to full speed and along to the goal ---
150: @section push-to-goal
150: cross
154:
166: cross
170:
182: cross
186:
198: cross
202:
214: cross
218:
230: cross
234:
246: cross
250:
262: cross
266:
278: cross
282:
294: cross
298:
310: cross
314:
326: cross
330:
342: cross
346:
358: cross
362:
374: cross
378:
390: cross
394:
406: cross
410:
422: cross
426:
438: cross
442:
454: cross
458:

# --- confirm progress: the skater should be grounded and rolling by now ---
460: @section confirm
460: @assert vpos ~ 60 +-6    # grounded (pushing keeps the skater on the deck)
470: @shot pushing-rolling    # eyeball frame for a human: skater mid-lesson
480: @note Pushing reliably reaches here. The PASS panel and its savedata write
480: @note land a bit later - extend this recipe and add an egress SaveWrite
480: @todo assert egress SaveWrite once the PASS-screen save frame is pinned
